  "name": "prv_in_pump_loop",
  "description": "A pump circulates around a loop that returns partly through an active PRV and partly through a bypass; the only reservoir hangs on a long small pipe that carries no flow. Verifies the loop and PRV flows, which a PRV flow lagged by one iteration (EPANET's scheme) approached too slowly to converge in 100 iterations (M4 differential test).",
  "source": "closed-form: tests/reference/derivations_status.py::prv_in_pump_loop (Darcy-Weisbach + Colebrook lines; PRV setpoint head z + p_set/(rho g) + v^2/(2g) on the outlet pipe; pump curve: scipy PchipInterpolator through the points; loop and PRV flows by scipy.optimize.fsolve)",
